Cannot get closer under the project's compiler: the C below matches byte for byte with gcc-2.7.2-kmc -G0 -mips3 -mgp32 -mfp32 -O2 -g3 (try_compiler), and the project's -O2 gives 320 on this exact source, so the remaining difference is the flag set, not the C. Shape: f32 args in $a1-$a3 (integer regs), arg4-6 are stack pointers; `if (temp == 1.0f) return 0.0f;` must come BEFORE the three divides (the `if (temp != 1.0f) {divide; return temp}` form puts the return-0 block in the wrong place). Suggested range 0x8001BFC4-0x8001C108 with -g3 (range check #55 started).

